# Line endings.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text vs binary; `eol=crlf` pins the working tree
# to CRLF on every platform, which is what this checkout already produced via
# `core.autocrlf=true`.
#
# This file exists because the tree had 13 files with MIXED endings (up to 32
# bare LF lines inside an 88-CRLF file). Mixed endings mean a one-line edit can
# produce a whole-file diff, `git blame` points at the wrong commit, and every
# `split('\n')` parser in this codebase leaves a stray `\r` on the last field of
# every line — including the JSONL readers for trajectories and audit records.
#
# Pinning it makes the normalization a property of the repository instead of a
# property of whoever happens to have autocrlf set.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Generated build output. Already gitignored, but saying so here stops a
# Windows check-in from ever staging one.
.next/        binary
node_modules/ binary
